#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0051 expect=skipped domain=VS
#note "VISIT is absent from VS, so Requirements.Variables.All [VISIT] gates the rule to SKIPPED. This asserts the SKIP, not a would-otherwise-fire -- the EC-53 fast path would answer an absent target with an empty BitSet anyway. Kept on VS deliberately: do NOT author any PMDA-SD0051 scenario on a TRIAL DESIGN, RELATIONSHIP or STUDY REFERENCE dataset, because that would pin behaviour the rule's own sheet cell contradicts and finding SD0051-F1 is unruled."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset VS class=FINDINGS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
---
S1 | VS | 001 | 1 | SYSBP | 1
S1 | VS | 002 | 1 | SYSBP | 1
S1 | VS | 003 | 1 | SYSBP | 2
